{"id": "sevt_01Dx3KTTH7xSLSDUvuhtFwRQ", "content": [{"text": "F-105 is a false positive. I created one ticket draft marking it not exploitable. A person still needs to review the draft before it's filed.\n\n| ID | Rule | Location | Verdict | Severity | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F-105 | SQL Injection | tests/fixtures/seed_db.py:10 | not_exploitable | none | The query does build an INSERT by joining strings, but the only values it uses come from the hardcoded `USERS` list (seed_db.py:3). The function's `path` argument is only used to open the database file. Nothing calls `seed()`, and the app (app/main.py) only has a static `/health` route, so no user input can reach this code. |\n\n**Suggested cleanup (optional):** switch to a parameterized query (`VALUES (?, ?)`) or exclude `tests/` from production scans so the scanner stops flagging it.\n\nI didn't read config.py's contents beyond confirming it doesn't refer to the fixture, and no secrets appear in the ticket.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-26T20:54:37.594731Z", "type": "agent.message"}
